A||||8||BillHarrison||Some questions for the Pros||||1||
Z||000000||BillHarrison||02-18-2001||05:12 PM||||Hi everyone.  A few quick questions.  Heres the background.  Bought an 86 GT, Automatic.  Also have in my possession 1990 Grand Prix Turbo, had a little mishap with another car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Looks like the fiero will benefit from it!  Questions are:<P>I will be using the 3.1 turbo in its entirety, including ecm and wiring (only real way to make it work right in my opinion) What tricks are needed to bolt in a FWD 3.1 (Note, the 3.1 turbo is almost IDENTICAL on the outside as a standard 3.1)<P>Second, After reading a lot of posts on trannys, I think that at first I will be using an ISUZU 5 speed from a 4 cyl car.  What flywheel will I need to use?  The Grand prix is an AUTO, so I have to get one somewhere else.  And from the Posts I read, the Grand Prix should be an internally balanced 3.1, so I will need the 88 and later flywheel.  But- with the Isuzu trans combo will I need one for the 4 cyl or 6?  <P>Thanks for the help in advance... this should be interesting when its done !||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||02-18-2001||07:56 PM||||Bill,<BR>Welcome to the forum. <BR>Looking forward to hearing about the results of your swap. The 3.1 turbo is really uncommon. <BR>I expect that your swap will be nearly a bolt-in. The trans will definitely bolt up. I believe the V-6 flywheel is the way to go. I have also heard that the MT flywheel for the 3.4 TDC is also useable. It's supposed to be just a bit thicker and waaayyyy cheaper. I have also heard that you should use the correct clutch and release bearing  for the tranny, as opposed to the engine. <BR>This is NOT the voice of experience speaking, but this is what I understand from reading many posts, over the past year or so.<BR>Best of luck.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||02-18-2001||11:19 PM||||There is an aluminum flywheel made. Do a search in the TD&Q for "aluminum flywheel" or something along those lines.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula 18||02-18-2001||11:31 PM||||Wow this sounds like it should be a schweet project. <BR>Not any flywheel from a v6 Fireo will work ok. I think that the 3.1L are internally bbalanced and need a 88 or later flywheel. <BR> <BR>One note... You will probally have ECM issues (at least PROM issues). Automatics computer don't like manual trannys. You might have to chage chips or atleast jump the shift select dingy like in 3800 swaps with manuals. <P>Just something you might want to think about. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||02-19-2001||07:48 AM||||I suggest that you write to or call Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory in Tony, Alabama (near Huntsville).<P>(256) 420-5391<BR>Fierofactory@juno.com<P>Sounds nice.<P>Good luck and welcome to the forum.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||02-19-2001||06:02 PM||||Yes use the clutch, P-Plate, & T.O. bearing for the Trans. I have the Isuzu hooked to my v6. The clutch releases great.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||4
Z||000006||BillHarrison||02-19-2001||10:04 PM||||Thanks.  I did notice quite a few posts about you and your V-6 isuzu.  Now I have heard from some sources use the V-6 clutch and pressure plate, and then isuzu T/O bearing and trans.  I would PREFER this, as I think I could get a beefier clutch, but if not, so be it.  Also, the 3.1 turbo will be internally balanced, so I will need an 88 & later flywheel off a?  V-6? Or a 4 cyl?  Which flywheel mates with the isuzu trans?||||reg||1
Z||000007||ray b||02-19-2001||11:56 PM||||flywheel stays with motor you need V-6. clutch type must be same as trans.<BR>only duck clutch fits in isisu trans but you need H D as you can find clutch.<BR>if you can find a getrag trans they are stronger plus can use V-6 clutch.<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||BillHarrison||02-20-2001||07:22 AM||||Thanks Ray... thats what I was looking for... Use the v-6 flywheel off an internally balanced engine. I agree, the Getrag would probably be a better choice.  But I have run into the fact that there are almost NO getrags available around here. Much less the parts to do a complete auto to manual conversion.  Isuzu 5 speeds on the other hand, are a dime a dozen.  I will see how they hold up, and if not bad I will stick with them.  If I shatter a few, I will upgrade.||||reg||1
